Z||000042||Black88GT||12-07-2000||03:22 PM||||The SD4 was about as reliable as a 1984 Ford Escort with a 200 shot of NOS...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000043||88formula||12-07-2000||05:47 PM||||You know the MR2 and the fiero are in different classes when you consider what you paid for them new. For example a new fiero formula started @ $11,000 in 1988 and the supercharged MR2 was about $16,400. That is a $5400 difference. It’s like comparing a Ford Mustang to a Chevy Corvette.<P>Stock for Stock the MR2 has it all over the fiero except in lateral g’s and styling for there same production years. The nice thing about the fiero is that it can be made a much better sports car than it is. <P>The choices are unlimited. The after market for the 60-degree v6 is very large and that engine responds well to traditional hot rod modifications. You can make an Iron Duke with over 300 horsepower (Cosworth). Pretty good for 70’s technology huh! You can swat in a high revving high horsepower light four cylinder (quad four), many types of turbocharged and supercharged six cylinders (supercharged and turbocharged 3.8-liter), a high buck high horsepower 32 valve v8 (Northstar), or a classic torque monster like the proven small block Chevy for motivation. I read somewhere that Archie is working on a kit to put an LS1 in a fiero. Can you imagine what that could do in a fiero! <P>You can have almost any body style you want through kit cars and the choices for suspension and brake upgrades for this car seem unlimited. You can even get high quality leather seats and other interior upgrades. Don't forget that you can upgrade the dash and interior to a more modern style through companies like PISA corp.<P>I also like to relative rareness of the fiero. The fiero is the underdog until you modify it to the way GM should have built them and then the tides change directions. At least GM made them one of the safest cars in a collision at than time. That is another plus for the fiero.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||1
